{"abstract":"Predicting career trajectories is a complex yet impactful task, offering significant benefits for personalized career counseling, recruitment optimization, and workforce planning. However, effective career path prediction (CPP) modeling faces challenges including highly variable career trajectories, free-text resume data, and limited publicly available benchmark datasets. In this study, we present a comprehensive comparative evaluation of CPP models—linear projection, multilayer perceptron (MLP), LSTM, and large language models (LLMs)—across multiple input settings and two recently introduced public datasets. Our contributions are threefold: (1) we propose novel model variants, including an MLP extension and a standardized LLM approach, (2) we systematically evaluate model performance across input types (titles only vs. title+description, standardized vs. free-text), and (3) we investigate the role of synthetic data and fine-tuning strategies in addressing data scarcity and improving model generalization. Additionally, we provide a detailed qualitative analysis of prediction behaviors across industries, career lengths, and transitions. Our findings establish new baselines, reveal the trade-offs of different modeling strategies, and offer practical insights for deploying CPP systems in real-world settings.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Senger, Elena","Campbell, Yuri","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828157"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich"],"keyword":["Career path prediction","LLM","Labor market","Recommendation","Synthetic data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward more realistic career path prediction evaluation and methods","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fdata.2025.1564521","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828157","ids":["itu-640078c3-3cde-48b4-a54f-985b7376a765"],"keyword":["LLM","career path prediction","labor market","recommendation","synthetic data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-09B6503596078F7A465596528060825D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fdata.2025.1564521","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"sengerpau","last":"Senger","name":"Senger, Elena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"campbellpau","last":"Campbell","name":"Campbell, Yuri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","name":"Plank, Barbara","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-640078c3-3cde-48b4-a54f-985b7376a765"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Toward more realistic career path prediction: evaluation and methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828157","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"There is an increasing trend towards evaluating NLP models with LLMs instead of human judgments, raising questions about the validity of these evaluations, as well as their reproducibility in the case of proprietary models. We provide JUDGE-BENCH, an extensible collection of 20 NLP datasets with human annotations covering a broad range of evaluated properties and types of data, and comprehensively evaluate 11 current LLMs, covering both open-weight and proprietary models, for their ability to replicate the annotations. Our evaluations show substantial variance across models and datasets. Models are reliable evaluators on some tasks, but overall display substantial variability depending on the property being evaluated, the expertise level of the human judges, and whether the language is human or model-generated. We conclude that LLMs should be carefully validated against human judgments before being used as evaluators.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Bavaresco, Anna","Bernardi, Raffaella","Bertolazzi, Leonardo","Elliott, Desmond","Fernández, Raquel","Gatt, Albert","Ghaleb, Esam","Giulianelli, Mario","Hanna, Michael","Koller, Alexander","Martins, André F. T.","Mondorf, Philipp","Neplenbroek, Vera","Pezzelle, Sandro","Plank, Barbara","Schlangen, David","Suglia, Alessandro","Surikuchi, Aditya K","Takmaz, Ece","Testoni, Alberto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828640"],"event":{"end":"2025-08-01","place":"Vienna, at","start":"2025-07-27","title":"63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Portugal","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","ETH Zürich","Heriot-Watt University","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Max Planck Institute of Psycholinguistics","Saarland University","University of Amsterdam","University of Lisbon","University of Potsdam","University of Trento","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["cs CL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"llms instead of human judges a large scale empirical study across 000000000020 nlp evaluation tasks","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.acl-short.20","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828640","ids":["ku-365bc5fd-20a6-4b9c-a5a1-73b7613d0ded"],"keyword":["cs.CL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7822F131A3BB61319BC900A0FE51B55F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/461118233/LLMs_instead_of_Human_Judges.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.acl-short.20","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of trento","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Trento","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Natural Language Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used"