EGE: A large scale Career Path Prediction Dataset","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828138","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Digital assistants perform well in high-resource languages like English, where tasks like slot and intent detection (SID) are well-supported. Many recent SID datasets start including multiple language varieties. However, it is unclear how realistic these translated datasets are. Therefore, we extend one such dataset, namely xSID-0.4, to include two underrepresented languages: Bavarian, a German dialect, and Lithuanian, a Baltic language. Both language variants have limited speaker populations and are often not included in multilingual projects. In addition to translations we provide ``natural'' queries to digital assistants generated by native speakers. We further include utterances from another dataset for Bavarian to build the richest SID dataset available today for a low-resource dialect without standard orthography. We then set out to evaluate models trained on English in a zero-shot scenario on our target language variants. Our evaluation reveals that translated data can produce overly optimistic scores. However, the error patterns in translated and natural datasets are highly similar. Cross-dataset experiments demonstrate that data collection methods influence performance, with scores lower than those achieved with single-dataset translations. This work contributes to enhancing SID datasets for underrepresented languages, yielding NaLiBaSID, a new evaluation dataset for Bavarian and Lithuanian.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Winkler, Miriam","Juozapaityte, Virginija","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776416"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich"],"keyword":["Zero shot learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"slot and intent detection resources for bavarian and lithuanian assessing translations vs natural queries to digital assistants","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.1297","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776416","identifier":[{"id":"85195904749","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-78e84191-d8f4-46cd-84d0-1d05c08bceb9"],"keyword":["Dataset creation and cross-dataset evaluation for SID","Low-resource languages and dialects","Multilingual natural language understanding","Slot filling and intent detection (SID)","Zero-shot learning"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C14CCA0E1340D738BF0EECDDF503D7C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.1297","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miriam","key":"winklerpau","last":"Winkler","name":"Winkler, Miriam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Virginija","key":"juozapaitytepau","last":"Juozapaityte","name":"Juozapaityte, Virginija","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicoletta","key":"calzolaripedh","last":"Calzolari","name":"Calzolari, Nicoletta","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Min-Yen","key":"kanpedh","last":"Kan","name":"Kan, Min-Yen","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Veronique","key":"hostepedh","last":"Hoste","name":"Hoste, Veronique","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alessandro","key":"lencipedh","last":"Lenci","name":"Lenci, Alessandro","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sakriani","key":"saktipedh","last":"Sakti","name":"Sakti, Sakriani","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nianwen","key":"xuepedh","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Nianwen","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"14898-14915","place":"Torino, Italia","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 Joint International Conference on Computational Linguistics, Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC-COLING 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-78e84191-d8f4-46cd-84d0-1d05c08bceb9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Slot and Intent Detection Resources for Bavarian and Lithuanian: Assessing Translations vs Natural Queries to Digital Assistants","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776416","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Annotation tools are the starting point for creating Natural Language Processing (NLP) datasets. There is a wide variety of tools available; setting up these tools is however a hindrance. We propose Eevee, an annotation tool focused on simplicity, efficiency, and ease of use. It can run directly in the browser (no setup required) and uses tab-separated files (as opposed to character offsets or task-specific formats) for annotation. It allows for annotation of multiple tasks on a single dataset and supports four task-types: sequence labeling, span labeling, text classification and seq2seq.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sorensen, Axel","Peng, Siyao","Plank, Barbara","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776398"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Munich Center for Machine Learning (MCML)"],"keyword":["Annotation tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eevee an easy annotation tool for natural language processing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85188684871","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776398","identifier":[{"id":"85188684871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4e17ab98-6c05-4726-ab59-a06e70afc823"],"keyword":["annotation tools","browser-based annotation","multi-task annotation","natural language processing datasets","tab-separated data format"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4742ACE9D4E795FA914371E2F8C4F69E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"munich center for machine learning","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Munich Center for Machine Learning (MCML)","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","name":"Sorensen, Axel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Siyao","key":"pengpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Siyao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"Van Der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","name_org":"Van Der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sophie","key":"henningpedh","last":"Henning","name":"Henning, Sophie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manfred","key":"stedepedh","last":"Stede","name":"Stede, Manfred","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"216-221","place":"St. Julians, Malta","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of The 18th Linguistic Annotation Workshop (LAW-XVIII)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4e17ab98-6c05-4726-ab59-a06e70afc823"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EEVEE: An Easy Annotation Tool for Natural Language Processing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776398","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Current language models require a lot of training data to obtain high performance. For Relation Classification (RC), many datasets are domain-specific, so combining datasets to obtain better performance is non-trivial. We explore a multi-domain training setup for RC, and attempt to improve performance by encoding domain information. Our proposed models improve > 2 Macro-F1 against the baseline setup, and our analysis reveals that not all the labels benefit the same: The classes which occupy a similar space across domains (i.e., their interpretation is close across them, for example “physical”) benefit the least, while domain-dependent relations (e.g., “part-of”) improve the most when encoding domain information.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bassignana, Elisa","Unmack Gascou, Viggo","Nøhr Laustsen, Frida","Kristensen, Gustav","Haahr Petersen, Marie","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747225"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DOMAIN","Multi domain training","Relation Classification","Robustness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to encode domain information in relation classification","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.728.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747225","identifier":[{"id":"85195940749","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4a4cff0a-a185-4211-9e3d-907605af2508"],"keyword":["Domain","Multi-domain training","Relation Classification","Robustness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-97A3E9F53EED0AA028ED91388E49D33E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.728.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Viggo","key":"unmackgascoupau","last":"Unmack Gascou","name":"Unmack Gascou, Viggo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Frida","key":"nøhrlaustsenpau","last":"Nøhr Laustsen","name":"Nøhr Laustsen, Frida","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gustav","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Gustav","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"haahrpetersenpau","last":"Haahr Petersen","name":"Haahr Petersen, Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"8301-8306","publisher":"European Language Resources Association","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 Joint International Conference on Computational Linguistics, Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC-COLING 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4a4cff0a-a185-4211-9e3d-907605af2508"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to Encode Domain Information in Relation Classification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747225","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Recent years have brought significant advances to Natural Language Processing (NLP), which enabled fast progress in the field of computational job market analysis. Core tasks in this application domain are skill extraction and classification from job postings. Because of its quick growth and its interdisciplinary nature, there is no exhaustive assessment of this field. This survey aims to fill this gap by providing a comprehensive overview of deep learning methodologies, datasets, and terminologies specific to NLP-driven skill extraction. Our comprehensive cataloging of publicly available datasets addresses the lack of consolidated information on dataset creation and characteristics. Finally, the focus on terminology addresses the current lack of consistent definitions for important concepts, such as hard and soft skills, and terms relating to skill extraction and classification.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Senger, Elena","Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730191"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich"],"keyword":["Deep Learning Methodologies","Job Market Analysis","Natural Language Processing NLP","Public Datasets","Skill Extraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep learning based computational job market analysis a survey on skill extraction and classification from job postings","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730191","ids":["itu-c29161fe-e38e-4086-b98a-cba9a4eefd88"],"keyword":["Deep Learning Methodologies","Job Market Analysis","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","Public Datasets","Skill Extraction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BB4DA2D1ED6BE5DC5E41DC7A0589DC0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.1/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"sengerpau","last":"Senger","name":"Senger, Elena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"1-15","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"1st Workshop on Natural Language Processing for Human Resources"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c29161fe-e38e-4086-b98a-cba9a4eefd88"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep Learning-based Computational Job Market Analysis: A Survey on Skill Extraction and Classification from Job Postings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730191","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The labor market is changing rapidly, prompting increased interest in the automatic extraction of occupational skills from text. With the advent of English benchmark job description datasets, there is a need for systems that handle their diversity well. We tackle the complexity in occupational skill datasets tasks---combining and leveraging multiple datasets for skill extraction, to identify rarely observed skills within a dataset, and overcoming the scarcity of skills across datasets. In particular, we investigate the retrieval-augmentation of language models, employing an external datastore for retrieving similar skills in a dataset-unifying manner. Our proposed method, Nearest Neighbor Occupational Skill Extraction (NNOSE) effectively leverages multiple datasets by retrieving neighboring skills from other datasets in the datastore. This improves skill extraction without additional fine-tuning. Crucially, we observe a performance gain in predicting infrequent patterns, with substantial gains of up to 30% span-F1 in cross-dataset settings.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob","Kan, Min-Yen","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730163"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National University of Singapore"],"keyword":["Benchmark job description datasets","Labor market","Language Models","Nearest Neighbor Occupational Skill Extraction NNOSE","Occupational skills extraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nnose nearest neighbor occupational skill extraction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.eacl-long.35.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730163","ids":["itu-2a506ba1-33c4-4015-bd87-ce515688f65b"],"keyword":["Benchmark job description datasets","Labor market","Language models","Nearest Neighbor Occupational Skill Extraction (NNOSE)","Occupational skills extraction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F0044AD8DC15DC05BAB3DBF221A38DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.eacl-long.35.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.eacl-long.35/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"national university of singapore","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"National University of Singapore","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Min-Yen","key":"kanpau","last":"Kan","name":"Kan, Min-Yen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"589-608","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"The 18th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2a506ba1-33c4-4015-bd87-ce515688f65b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"NNOSE: Nearest Neighbor Occupational Skill Extraction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730163","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In Natural Language Processing, entity linking (EL) has centered around Wikipedia, but yet remains underexplored for the job market domain. Disambiguating skill mentions can help us get insight into the current labor market demands. In this work, we are the first to explore EL in this domain, specifically targeting the linkage of occupational skills to the ESCO taxonomy (le Vrang et al., 2014). Previous efforts linked coarse-grained (full) sentences to a corresponding ESCO skill. In this work, we link more fine-grained span-level mentions of skills. We tune two high-performing neural EL models, a bi-encoder (Wu et al., 2020) and an autoregressive model (Cao et al., 2021), on a synthetically generated mention–skill pair dataset and evaluate them on a human-annotated skill-linking benchmark. Our findings reveal that both models are capable of linking implicit mentions of skills to their correct taxonomy counterparts. Empirically, BLINK outperforms GENRE in strict evaluation, but GENRE performs better in loose evaluation (accuracy@k).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730204"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ESCO Taxonomy","Entity Linking","Natural Language Processing","Neural models","Occupational Skills"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"entity linking in the job market domain","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730204","ids":["itu-f13178df-cafe-4855-86ee-f18db7fc8afa"],"keyword":["ESCO Taxonomy","Entity Linking","Natural Language Processing","Neural Models","Occupational Skills"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-84C3025A24589417B7A4C7C62C7964B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.28/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"410-419","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"The 18th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f13178df-cafe-4855-86ee-f18db7fc8afa"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Entity Linking in the Job Market Domain","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730204","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
