{"abstract":"We present UDP, the first training-free parser for Universal Dependencies (UD). Our algorithm is based on PageRank and a small set of specific dependency head rules. UDP features two-step decoding to guarantee that function words are attached as leaf nodes. The parser requires no training, and it is competitive with a delexicalized transfer system. UDP offers a linguistically sound unsupervised alternative to cross-lingual parsing for UD. The parser has very few parameters and distinctly robust to domain change across languages.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Martínez Alonso, Héctor","Agic, Zeljko","Plank, Barbara","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383261"],"event":{"acronym":"EACL","title":"Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Paris Diderot University","University of Groningen"],"keyword":["Cross lingual parsing","Dependency head rules","PageRank","Training free parsing","Universal Dependencies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parsing universal dependencies without training","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.aclweb.org/anthology/E17-1022","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383261","identifier":[{"id":"85021642092","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8804f2e1-6956-4dc4-a873-1fef7583c294"],"keyword":["Cross-lingual parsing","Dependency head rules","PageRank","Training-free parsing","Universal Dependencies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Loca